## JVM Basics

JDK (Java Development Kit):
Used for developing Java applications. It contains compiler (javac), JRE, and tools.

JRE (Java Runtime Environment):
Used to run Java programs. It contains JVM and core libraries.

JVM (Java Virtual Machine):
Executes Java bytecode and makes Java platform-independent.

Bytecode:
Intermediate code generated after compilation. JVM converts it into machine code.

Write Once, Run Anywhere:
Java code compiles to bytecode, which can run on any system having a JVM.
